            <ArticleTitle>Giant arachnoid granulation mimicking dural sinus thrombosis in a boy with headache: MRI.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>181-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report MRI and angiographic findings of an unusual giant arachnoid granulation in the left sigmoid sinus in a boy with headache. Its signal intensity was lower than that of cerebral cortex on T1-weighted images and higher on T2 weighting, mimicking dural sinus thrombosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
